WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.187 --> 00:00:06.187
- I've not looked at myself in
a mirror for over a year now.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.600
- [Mark] And why is that?

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.750
- [Jerry] I just don't.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:21.580
- [Mark] So do you ever get
angry over what happened

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:22.413
to you Jerry?

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.257
- Not really, no, no.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:31.630
They say, I can't change
it, gotta accept it.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.750
- [Mark] If you could say something

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.243
to the person that shot
you, what would you say?

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.442
- I still love you.

00:00:44.442 --> 00:00:45.442
Forgiveness.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:50.313
- [Mark] That's the only way, isn't it?

00:00:54.508 --> 00:00:57.983
- The Bible said, "Vengeance are mine's."

00:01:09.553 --> 00:01:10.460
- [Mark] What do you wish

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:11.860
the world understood better?

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:16.400
What do you think a lot of
people don't quite understand?

00:01:20.102 --> 00:01:21.552
- Maybe living, a lot

00:01:21.552 --> 00:01:24.802
of people don't understand living life.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:33.563
With life you have to go
through the highs and lows,

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:35.783
ups and downs.

00:01:39.978 --> 00:01:44.978
They say, every day the sun
don't shine, it has to rain.

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.567
- [Mark] Do you go to church every Sunday?

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.220
- Sometimes they bring
church out in the street

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:57.263
and I go there.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:01.850
I was raised in the
church as a little boy,

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:02.800
I had to go to church every Sunday.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.140
- [Mark] Oh so you've
always been religious?

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.859
- My mother made us go to church.

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:09.210
Sunday school in the morning

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:11.757
and all the way til two
o'clock in the evening.

00:02:11.757 --> 00:02:12.630
- [Mark] And do you find

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:15.200
that religious background helped you deal

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.314
with what happened with you?

00:02:16.314 --> 00:02:18.730
- Definitely, it does, yes.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:19.563
- [Mark] 'Cause your attitude today

00:02:19.563 --> 00:02:21.713
is so light and pleasant and positive.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:26.407
- I keep my trust in God.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.370
- [Mark] Yeah you're an amazing guy.

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:39.640
I mean I think your
attitude is an inspiration

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:40.473
to so many people.

00:02:40.473 --> 00:02:45.160
- See, I have every reason
to be mad at the world.

00:02:47.777 --> 00:02:48.960
I have an excuse.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.627
I have an excuse to be mad at the world

00:02:50.627 --> 00:02:54.130
and everything 'cause of
this right here, but I don't.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:58.144
I could give up, I'm not giving up.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.477
I can't give up.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.270
My mind and heart won't let me.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.468
- [Mark] Did you ever do
drugs during your life?

00:03:15.468 --> 00:03:16.598
- Smoked weed.

00:03:16.598 --> 00:03:18.570
- [Mark] You smoked weed?

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:19.403
- Yeah.

00:03:19.403 --> 00:03:21.060
- [Mark] You never did
crack or anything heavier?

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.520
- No, no, no.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.780
- [Mark] 'Cause I had heard a story

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:29.280
that the reason you got shot
was because of a crack debt

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.660
and somebody shot you and
it was some different story.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:33.493
- Yeah.

00:03:33.493 --> 00:03:35.365
(laughs)

00:03:36.757 --> 00:03:39.393
One girl said I broke
into somebody's house,

00:03:40.797 --> 00:03:42.675
and I took their drugs
and shot me coming out.

00:03:42.675 --> 00:03:43.508
(laughs)

00:03:43.508 --> 00:03:44.777
I said, "Ooo-wee!."

00:03:44.777 --> 00:03:45.610
I've heard all kinds of stories.

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:47.500
- [Mark] People love
to hear stories right?

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:48.718
Be able to make stories.

00:03:48.718 --> 00:03:51.148
- "He was in a gang."

00:03:51.148 --> 00:03:52.481
I was in a gang.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:54.659
- [Mark] They said you were in a gang?

00:03:54.659 --> 00:03:56.356
- Ooh, you hear so many stories.

00:03:56.356 --> 00:03:57.239
- [Mark] But you were never in a gang?

00:03:57.239 --> 00:03:58.765
- No, I was never in a gang.

00:03:58.765 --> 00:03:59.740
You hear all kinds of.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.510
- [Mark] This is what I'm
learning now with social media

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:06.150
is people love to create little
stories for whatever reason,

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:07.530
and there's multiple reasons for it.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.210
That people love to create
stories to defame people,

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:12.003
to tarnish their image.

00:04:12.983 --> 00:04:14.550
And it's fueled by jealousy,

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:17.173
or it's fueled by something, who knows.

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:21.273
- Now, the people who told you that,

00:04:21.273 --> 00:04:24.260
ask them "how do you know?"

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:26.510
- [Mark] 'Cause he said
somebody that lived

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:28.378
in the apartment building,
there's always some credible.

00:04:28.378 --> 00:04:30.237
- And then, "how do they now?"

00:04:30.237 --> 00:04:31.120
- [Mark] (laughs)

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:31.953
No I know.

00:04:31.953 --> 00:04:33.480
- See what I'm saying?

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:34.850
How do they know?

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:37.847
- [Mark] No, I'm learning
that just 'cause a story

00:04:37.847 --> 00:04:40.017
is voiced doesn't mean it's true.

00:04:40.017 --> 00:04:44.650
- You hear all kinds of stories.

00:04:46.128 --> 00:04:48.020
I robbed a drug man.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.573
Oh, I've heard it all.

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:55.904
- [Mark] So, religion plays a
huge role in your life, right?

00:04:55.904 --> 00:04:57.689
- Definitely, it's got to.

00:04:57.689 --> 00:04:59.740
If everybody had religion

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:03.347
in their life this
would be a better world.

00:05:04.315 --> 00:05:05.990
- [Jerry] Yeah, religion.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.073
Oh man, made me stronger.

00:05:12.602 --> 00:05:14.352
God takes care of me.

00:05:20.902 --> 00:05:24.050
Life would be most beautiful,
you'd see life most beautiful.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.466
- [Mark] You ever get depressed?

00:05:25.466 --> 00:05:26.299
- [Jerry] Huh?

00:05:26.299 --> 00:05:27.132
- [Mark] You ever get depressed?

00:05:27.132 --> 00:05:29.198
- [Jerry] Give me an example,
exactly what depressed

00:05:29.198 --> 00:05:30.281
is like what?

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:36.480
- [Mark] Like just feeling
down, feeling like your life

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.200
is not working out the
way you wanted it to.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:42.113
You pity yourself, you
feel like you're a victim.

00:05:43.849 --> 00:05:45.260
- [Jerry] No.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:46.290
- [Mark] I don't hear any of that,

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.390
I've talked to you how many
times now, countless times.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:50.040
I've never heard any of that from you.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.540
I'm just asking these questions

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:53.127
because my viewers will be like,

00:05:53.127 --> 00:05:55.040
"You gotta be depressed
sometimes, you gotta get angry,

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.280
you gotta be something."

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.226
- [Jerry] I get mad, but not because

00:05:58.226 --> 00:06:00.010
of what happened to me, though.

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:01.206
- [Mark] Just because you're human.

00:06:01.206 --> 00:06:02.039
- [Jerry] Yeah human.

00:06:02.039 --> 00:06:04.373
If you're human you'll get mad at stuff.

00:06:04.373 --> 00:06:09.268
If I had a chance to live
my life over again I'd want

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:11.552
to live it the same way I'm living it now.

00:06:11.552 --> 00:06:12.385
- [Mark] Including the.

00:06:12.385 --> 00:06:13.481
- [Jerry] Everything, yeah.

00:06:13.481 --> 00:06:14.787
- [Mark] Everything.

00:06:14.787 --> 00:06:16.187
That's a beautiful attitude.

00:06:18.782 --> 00:06:21.333
- [Jerry] See I got to keep on living.

00:06:25.023 --> 00:06:28.387
They say the mind is a
terrible thing to lose.

00:06:28.387 --> 00:06:30.237
- [Mark] And your mind is 100% there.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:35.450
You're lucky that, whatever
part of your brain you lost.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:36.407
- Front brain.

00:06:36.407 --> 00:06:38.750
- [Mark] It's not really a huge.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:40.020
How are you impaired?

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:42.300
'Cause you walk, you talk, you think,

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.133
you're attitude is great.

00:06:43.133 --> 00:06:44.630
I mean what do you think.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.500
- My patience is very short.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:47.518
- [Mark] Your patience is short?

00:06:47.518 --> 00:06:48.351
- That's it.

00:06:48.351 --> 00:06:49.230
- [Mark] Join the club.

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:50.063
- Yeah.

00:06:51.632 --> 00:06:53.049
And my stability.

00:06:53.992 --> 00:06:55.038
- [Mark] Your what?

00:06:55.038 --> 00:06:56.038
- Stability.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:59.177
I'll be walking and I'll
stumble to the side a bit.

00:06:59.177 --> 00:07:00.189
- [Mark] Oh your stability?

00:07:00.189 --> 00:07:01.689
- Stability, yeah.

00:07:02.641 --> 00:07:05.990
See, they took my front brain out,

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:09.459
but if it was my back brain, I'd be dead.

00:07:09.459 --> 00:07:10.580
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.940
- Because your back brain
controls your whole body.

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:17.796
It helps you see, move, all that stuff.

00:07:17.796 --> 00:07:22.400
It goes through the back brain.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:26.148
See when boxers fight and
get hit in the chin and fall,

00:07:26.148 --> 00:07:28.315
it rattles the back brain.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:44.950
- [Mark] What was the
best time of your life?

00:07:48.475 --> 00:07:50.640
- When I went to BYU.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:52.382
- [Mark] You went to BYU?

00:07:52.382 --> 00:07:53.920
- I played basketball, right?

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:57.380
They had all the top high
school basketball players

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:00.183
in the United States.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:03.480
At BYU, two weeks the played
a tournament over there.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:06.750
That's where I met Danny Ainge up there,

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.180
but he wasn't Danny Ainge who was playing

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:10.960
with the basketball.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:11.930
- [Mark] Who's that, Danny Ainge?

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:13.110
- Yeah, he wasn't Danny Ainge then

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:14.660
while he was going to BYU.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:15.753
- [Mark] Oh I see.

00:08:15.753 --> 00:08:17.953
- And you know, Danny
Ainge played baseball.

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:20.580
For the Toronto Blue Jays.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.720
But he didn't work out, right.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.200
So, he was drafted by the Boston Celtics

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:27.410
and he left baseball
to go play basketball.

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:30.130
- [Mark] Yeah you were a great
basketball player, right?

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:31.675
- Yeah.

00:08:31.675 --> 00:08:32.759
- [Mark] You had a scholarship?

00:08:32.759 --> 00:08:35.040
- I didn't do good in school.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.436
- [Mark] Oh so your
grades were not so great?

00:08:36.436 --> 00:08:37.269
- Yeah.

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:41.783
- [Mark] But you're tall enough.

00:08:42.962 --> 00:08:43.795
Six four?

00:08:43.795 --> 00:08:45.984
- Six four, yeah.

00:08:45.984 --> 00:08:46.817
- [Mark] Yeah you look athletic.

00:08:46.817 --> 00:08:48.560
You've lost some weight
though you told me.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:49.750
- Yeah I have.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.030
I've got to get that weight back.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:52.623
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:08:52.623 --> 00:08:53.610
- I'd really feel more comfortable

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:54.443
if I could get that weight back.

00:08:54.443 --> 00:08:56.616
- [Mark] So your life
today, you have housing?

00:08:56.616 --> 00:08:58.340
- Oh, I'm glad I have that.

00:08:58.340 --> 00:08:59.770
- [Mark] Yeah it's a nice
little place you got,

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:01.230
nice building.

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:04.870
I mean it's still a
skid row housing thing,

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:07.099
but it's one of the nicest ones
in the neighborhood I think.

00:09:07.099 --> 00:09:10.510
- Yeah, what I like
about it is the security.

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:11.900
- [Mark] Yeah very secure.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.001
Hard to get into that building.

00:09:13.001 --> 00:09:14.670
- That's right, that's
what I love about it.

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:15.503
- [Mark] I was just telling them,

00:09:15.503 --> 00:09:16.410
I'm coming to meet Jerry
and they let me in.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:17.401
But other than that.

00:09:17.401 --> 00:09:20.337
- Yeah, it's very hard.

00:09:20.337 --> 00:09:22.391
But they know you there, Mark.

00:09:22.391 --> 00:09:23.724
Gary down there.

00:09:25.547 --> 00:09:29.214
- [Mark] What do you
think you need in life?

00:09:31.687 --> 00:09:35.211
- I've got God in my life, so let me see.

00:09:35.211 --> 00:09:36.793
I don't know.

00:09:36.793 --> 00:09:39.951
I need a radio, that's what I need.

00:09:39.951 --> 00:09:42.310
- [Mark] Let's go get
you a radio right now.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:43.170
I'm gonna get you radio.

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:44.003
- Okay.

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:48.294
- [Mark] That's easy.

00:09:48.294 --> 00:09:50.097
- I just want a little
pocket one like that.

00:09:50.097 --> 00:09:51.250
- [Mark] So you can carry it with you?

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:52.530
- So I can put it in my shirt, yeah.

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:53.363
- [Mark] Okay.

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:55.843
That's it?

00:09:55.843 --> 00:09:58.063
- Yeah.

00:09:59.714 --> 00:10:03.170
I've seen no football games this year,

00:10:04.969 --> 00:10:06.760
and no basketball games.

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:07.593
- [Mark] You don't want TV?

00:10:07.593 --> 00:10:08.946
- I can't see TV.

00:10:08.946 --> 00:10:09.917
- [Mark] You can't see it?

00:10:09.917 --> 00:10:10.750
Vision's not so good.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.820
- My vision's not too good.

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:13.703
- [Mark] But radio would
do the trick for you?

00:10:13.703 --> 00:10:17.193
- Yeah, I listen to KNX news.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.150
You ever heard KNX news?

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:21.533
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:10:21.533 --> 00:10:23.210
- You give us 20 minutes,
we give you the world.

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:24.340
- [Mark] Yeah you get everything.

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:27.113
You get all the
information you could have.

00:10:28.308 --> 00:10:29.505
So, do you have a cell phone?

00:10:29.505 --> 00:10:30.338
- No.

00:10:30.338 --> 00:10:31.793
- [Mark] Do you have a bank account?

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:33.620
- Yes.

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:34.453
- [Mark] You do?

00:10:34.453 --> 00:10:39.453
- Yeah.

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:40.543
- [Mark] Are you saving money

00:10:40.543 --> 00:10:42.765
or do you just have enough just to get by?

00:10:42.765 --> 00:10:45.182
- Just to get by, day by day.

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:48.683
- [Mark] Anything you'd like to do

00:10:48.683 --> 00:10:50.743
in your life before your days are done?

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:53.893
Any dreams, any goals, any like that?

00:10:53.893 --> 00:10:58.820
- Yes, I want to take a
bite out of the Big Apple.

00:10:58.820 --> 00:10:59.888
- [Mark] You wanna go to New York?

00:10:59.888 --> 00:11:01.471
- Yeah, the Big Apple.

00:11:01.471 --> 00:11:03.540
I've always wanted to go there.

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:04.994
I'd love to go to New York.

00:11:04.994 --> 00:11:07.095
- [Mark] Yeah, New York's a great city.

00:11:07.095 --> 00:11:10.940
- I've never been in
the snow before either.

00:11:11.789 --> 00:11:12.831
I've never been in the snow.

00:11:12.831 --> 00:11:14.063
I'd like it in the snow.

00:11:14.063 --> 00:11:14.896
- [Mark] You wanna see it in the snow?

00:11:14.896 --> 00:11:16.797
- I'd like to see it in the snow,

00:11:16.797 --> 00:11:20.040
but they say it's real cold out there.

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:21.960
- [Mark] Yeah it's cold as shit.

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:22.793
- Yeah.

00:11:22.793 --> 00:11:23.626
- [Mark] In the winter.

00:11:23.626 --> 00:11:25.724
- They say you have to
keep the defroster running

00:11:25.724 --> 00:11:27.700
or else you'll freeze.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.843
- [Mark] Well, that's
when it's extreme cold.

00:11:32.983 --> 00:11:33.960
You've got a drivers license or some kind

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:35.203
of ID to get on a plane?

00:11:35.203 --> 00:11:36.490
- I've got a California ID.

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:37.459
- [Mark] Yeah, okay.

00:11:37.459 --> 00:11:38.495
That's all you need.

00:11:38.495 --> 00:11:41.535
- You know how, you take
planes and stuff like that?

00:11:41.535 --> 00:11:43.680
- [Mark] Oh yeah, I fly all the time.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.630
Let me know when to take you to New York.

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:46.580
Do you want to go to New York with me?

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:47.551
- Yeah.

00:11:47.551 --> 00:11:49.051
- [Mark] Let's go to New York.

00:11:50.176 --> 00:11:52.463
- You need a passport
to leave the country?

00:11:52.463 --> 00:11:53.486
- [Mark] I'm sorry.

00:11:53.486 --> 00:11:55.230
- A passport to leave the country, right?

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:56.936
- [Mark] You need a passport
to go to another country.

00:11:56.936 --> 00:11:59.692
- You can get passports too?

00:11:59.692 --> 00:12:00.598
- [Mark] I'm sorry.

00:12:00.598 --> 00:12:01.490
- Is it hard to get a passport?

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:02.730
- [Mark] No it's easy to get a passport.

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:04.140
